CRITICAL INSIGHTS CAPTURED
================================================================================

1. Dedicated executor ≠ Bypass workflow engine
   - These are orthogonal concerns
   - Executor location is infrastructure
   - Workflow execution is application logic

2. Steep workflow engine is NON-NEGOTIABLE
   - Handles ForEach iterations
   - Manages variable chaining
   - Enables service abstraction
   - Maintains consistency with SeisSol

3. Service script provides polymorphism
   - Single entry point (run_hpo.py)
   - Location-transparent (works on-prem and cloud)
   - Runner classes encapsulate implementation

4. Threading model matches SeisSol
   - One thread per workflow
   - Threads block and exit naturally
   - No complex state management needed

5. Thread lifecycle is automatic
   - Created when workflow arrives
   - Blocks during workflow.execute()
   - Exits when function returns
   - No manual cleanup required

